# Normalise line endings.
#
# The repo currently has mixed endings: most files are CRLF, but any file edited
# on macOS/Linux tooling becomes LF, which turns a two-line change into a
# whole-file diff and makes review painful.
#
# This declares LF as canonical in the repository. Existing files are NOT
# rewritten until someone runs a one-off renormalisation:
#
#   git add --renormalize . && git commit -m "chore: normalise line endings"
#
# That is deliberately left as a separate, reviewable commit because it touches
# every file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
